# T6i: the current song on real flash. Boot with an empty store builds the song from the project
# and marks it dirty; an edit made in LIVE (a key assignment, as T10 will do) is part of the
# current song; leaving LIVE, stopping and waiting autosaves it to slot 0 (the project first, the
# song after it); a reboot finds the stored song (and LIVE uses it, no fresh mapping).
wait 300
# --- boot: the store is empty, so the song is the project mapping, dirty ---
expect songloaded 0
expect songdirty 1
expect songsaves 0
expect songwrites 0
# --- change a key assignment in LIVE ---
turn ALGO 2
tapkey w0
turn ALGO -2
press PLAY
wait 700
release PLAY
wait 20
expect mode 1
assignkey 0 12
expect keyclip0 12
expect songdirty 1
# while LIVE is active, nothing is written, however long it waits
wait 6000
expect songsaves 0
expect songwrites 0
# --- leave LIVE and stop: the autosave writes the song ---
press PLAY
wait 700
release PLAY
wait 20
expect mode 0
wait 5000
expect songdirty 0
expect songsaves 1
expect songwrites >0
shot t6i_song.png
# --- reboot: slot 0 is the current song, assignments and all ---
reboot
expect songloaded 1
expect songdirty 0
expect keyclip0 12
